' Hayai ticket lifecycle on a time axis (ZeroSignalEscrow.algo.ts, SPEC §3a/§3b).
' Companion to the sequence-oriented flow-escrow-payment.puml. Units on the time
' axis are unix seconds (compared against Global.latestTimestamp on-chain).
'
' Consensus-verified-operator + prepaid-MBR-pool design (SPEC.md "Operator
' authentication" + "Settlement asset model"): open() and settle() authenticate
' the operator via Algorand consensus (no in-contract ed25519verify_bare); only
' protest() uses the contract-side receipt-sig verify.
'
' ========== Phase legend ==========
'   [A] reserve       off-chain only; node builds ticket_id, K_response,
'                     commit_k, signs ticket (off-chain audit), and
'                     pre-signs gtxn[1] of the open group at fee =
'                     2 * minTxnFee. Returns Ticket + presigned_open_txn
'                     + wrapped_response_key. No escrow state yet.
'   [B] open          2-tx atomic group lands on chain (no feePayment leg):
'                       gtxn[0] payer usdcPayment   USDC max_price       fee=0
'                       gtxn[1] operator AppCall    open(...)            fee=2*minTxnFee
'                     contract open() asserts Txn.sender == nodeSigning (the
'                     serving node's key from the (operatorId,nodeId) node box;
'                     consensus-verified), draws one box-MBR slot from the
'                     payer's prepaid pool (openTickets++), and stamps
'                     status=STATUS_OPEN. Payer ALGO net cost: 0 microALGO.
'   [C] inference     sealed req/resp (see flow-request-response); operator
'                     emits a signed UsageReceipt and an operator-signed
'                     atomic settle group (gtxn[0]) bound to a payer-ack
'                     gtxn[1] template.
'   [D] claim/ack     normally a single atomic broadcast: proxy signs gtxn[1]
'                     (payer ack) against the operator's pre-signed gtxn[0],
'                     submits as a 2-tx group. gtxn[0] flips OPEN ->
'                     PENDING_SETTLE; gtxn[1] (matching args, opposite side)
'                     finalizes and deletes the box. Same-side re-claim with
'                     matching args is an idempotent no-op (resolves the
'                     watchdog race).
'                     Operator-side settlement driver acts as a watchdog
'                     fallback only — fires standalone after
'                     hayai.settlement_watchdog_seconds (default 30s) if
'                     the proxy never broadcast.
'   [E] expires_at    unix-second boundary (TicketRecord.expiresAt); no new
'                     inference admitted. settle() / protest() still legal
'                     while status is OPEN or PENDING_SETTLE.
'   [F] +grace        expires_at + settlementGraceSeconds reached.
'                     settleLapsed() now finalizes a pending operator claim
'                     that the payer never responded to.
'                     refundInactive() refunds the payer when no operator
'                     claim was ever posted (or only a payer-side claim).
'                     settle() (the two-party happy path) is rejected past
'                     this boundary.
'   [G] terminal      ticket deleted (atomic match, watchdog standalone +
'                     later finalize, settleLapsed, or refundInactive),
'                     or STATUS_FROZEN (mismatch / protest, awaits
'                     off-chain arbitration).
'
' ========== Design notes ==========
'   1. Co-signed settle removes the race between settle() and protest().
'      Finalization requires both sides on-chain; happy path is the atomic
'      group, where both calls land in a single broadcast. `protest()` is
'      strictly the structured-evidence path — silent disagreement via a
'      mismatched second settle() call also freezes the ticket.
'
'   2. Operator absorbs all per-request ALGO fees via fee pooling.
'      open() gtxn[1] fee = 2*minTxnFee covers the whole open group;
'      settle() fees are SIZED to the disbursement inners that actually fire
'      (SettleInnerCount = 0..3, escrow/fee.go). Atomic gtxn[0] =
'      (2 outer + SettleInnerCount + gapOpUps)*minTxnFee — the grouped path
'      adds no base op-up, so a paid ticket = 5, a free model = 2, ~6 worst
'      case. Standalone settle / settleLapsed adds a base op-up:
'      (1 outer + SettleInnerCount + 1 + gapOpUps)*minTxnFee — 5 paid, 2 free.
'      Payer ALGO net cost on the happy path is 0 microALGO; only
'      refundInactive (2*minTxnFee) and protest (4*minTxnFee) are
'      payer-fee-bearing paths.
'
'   3. settleLapsed is the operator's timeout fallback.
'      Callable by anyone after expires_at + settlementGraceSeconds, but only
'      when a PENDING_SETTLE claim was posted by the operator. If no claim
'      exists (or the pending side is the payer), refundInactive is the only
'      post-deadline path and the payer recovers the full max_price + MBR.
'
'   4. settlement_grace_seconds semantics.
'      Payer-silence window in seconds: how long after expires_at the
'      operator waits before force-finalizing via settleLapsed. Happy-path
'      settle() still must land before the same deadline.
'
'   5. asOperator ABI arg.
'      settle(ticketId, amountCharged, receiptDigest, asOperator) lets the
'      same Algorand account act as both operator and payer (e.g. operator
'      testing their own deployment). The contract pins authorization on
'      the arg: asOperator=true requires Txn.sender == t.nodeSigning
'      (the serving node's key); asOperator=false requires Txn.sender == t.payer.
'
'   6. protest() authorization + evidence.
'      protest() is the payer's one-call freeze primitive: callable while
'      status is OPEN or PENDING_SETTLE, it runs an in-contract
'      ed25519verify_bare over the operator's receipt sig and carries a
'      length-capped dispute_excerpt. open() and settle() instead authenticate
'      the operator via Algorand consensus (no in-contract ed25519verify_bare).
'      A FROZEN ticket resolves through the admin/arbiter path off-chain.

@startuml
title Ticket lifecycle on a time axis (ZeroSignalEscrow, SPEC §3a/§3b)

skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam noteBorderColor #C0A000

concise "Phase"         as PH
robust  "Ticket.status" as TS
concise "Operator"      as OP
concise "Payer"         as PAY
concise "Anyone"        as ANY

@0
PH is "-"
TS is none
OP is idle
PAY is idle
ANY is idle

@10
PH is "A: reserve"
OP is "reserve\n+ pre-sign gtxn[1]"
PAY -> OP : \nPOST /v1/zs/reserve\n(payer_addr, proxy_recipient)
note top of OP : returns Ticket + wrapped_response_key\n+ presigned_open_txn (gtxn[1], fee=2*minTxnFee)

@25
PH is "B: open"
TS is OPEN
OP is "await req"
PAY -> TS : 2-tx open group\n(operator-signed gtxn[1] + payer-signed gtxn[0] usdcPayment)
note bottom of PAY : payer ALGO fee = 0\n(operator's gtxn[1] fee pools the group; box MBR from prepaid pool)

@40
PH is "C: inference"
OP is serve
PAY -> OP : sealed request
OP -> PAY : sealed response\n+ UsageReceipt + presigned settle group

@70
PH is "D: claim/ack"
TS is PENDING_SETTLE
OP is "watchdog\n(30s default)"
PAY -> TS : atomic settle group\n(gtxn[0] op first-half + gtxn[1] payer ack)
note top of PAY : single broadcast in the happy path —\noperator's gtxn[0] flips status, payer's gtxn[1]\nfinalizes (idempotent no-op on same-side\nmatching re-claim).

@90
note bottom of OP : if proxy never broadcasts, watchdog fires\nstandalone at fee=(1+SettleInnerCount+1+gapOpUps)*minTxnFee\n(5 paid, 2 free) after settlement_watchdog_seconds.
OP -> TS : settle(asOperator=true) — standalone

@105
PH is "E: expires_at"

@125
PH is "F: +grace"
ANY is "lapsed / refund"
ANY -> TS : settleLapsed() OR refundInactive()
note top of ANY : settle() rejected past deadline.\nsettleLapsed: pending operator claim\n(finalizes to operator).\nrefundInactive: no operator claim\n(full refund to payer).

@155
PH is "G: terminal"
TS is "deleted (match / lapse / refund) or FROZEN"
OP is "-"
PAY is "-"
ANY is "-"

highlight 25 to 70 #E8F4FF
highlight 70 to 105 #F0E8FF
highlight 105 to 125 #FFF4CC
highlight 125 to 155 #FFE8E8

@enduml
